[block'ORD-0003-recovery'
  [ctx'the spec of EMS-002','.guidelines/.orders/EMS-002/EMS-002.pgml']
  [onlyif'ORD-0002 closed']
  [tgt'glyph-vpath: the recovery index, layer 7 of .plan section 0, by the content']
  [cnst'recovery runs at build time, only for a Markdown section that no rule of the NodeID reached; its successor is the new section whose body has the largest line-set Jaccard with the old one, at least 0.5 and unique']
  [cnst'recovery is not identity: the successor keeps its own NodeID, and the old path and the old NodeID point at it as recovered, with the score']
  [cnst'the old text comes from the cache of the last build, then from git at HEAD, each taken only when its fingerprint equals the one the index holds; with neither, the section goes unrecovered and the build says so']
  [cnst'the cache and the log of misses live beside the index and out of git, as the session files of the regency plugin do']
  [nt'the cache answers what git cannot: a second build before a commit, and a checkout whose line endings differ from the commit']
  [nev'recovery by the path: precision 35.7 percent, INTAKE-VIRTUAL-PATH section 23']
  [val'the recovery','a heading renamed while its body changes is found again by its old path and by its old NodeID; a deletion is not, and two successors that tie are not']
  [val'the index miss','every answer through a recovery warns with its score, never blocks, and is written to the log of misses; misses reads the log']
  [val'the gate','npm run check refuses a source declared by a recovered path, naming the successor, and an index whose recoveries point at nothing or at a live path, each seen failing before it counts']
];
